Z||000000||CHUCKVH||06-12-2001||09:28 PM||||Hey Ogre, did you ever finish your cruise control addition?  My commute is killing me, I would love to add cruise to my 88 duke.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||06-13-2001||06:26 AM||||J.C. Whitney (and others I would imagine) sells an add on cruise control. I think someone on here installed one and said it was fine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-13-2001||07:11 PM||||Unlike other Fiero, the 87-88 4 cyl ECM contains the cruise logic. This makes the cruise sort of a drop in. You only need the stalk wiring and the servor. Much simpler system than the ones with external module.<P>Due to recent surgery I have been unable to get to the wrecking yards to dig out the parts. I have most of the data I need I just haven't been able to collect all the hardware and make a working setup yet. I don't know when that will be. ((I found out the hardway this week that I'm not up to big walk/climb/crawl projects....))<P>If you are in a hurry one of the aftermarket kits will have to be your answer for now.||||reg||1
Z||000003||CHUCKVH||06-13-2001||09:27 PM||||Is the servo the same for the 2.5 and 2.8?  What about for other GM products of the same vintage?  The stalk is no problem, they aren't too expensive to buy new.  I had hoped that most of the wiring would have already been in the harness, just because it seems that it would have been cheaper for GM to make one harness for all cars, than to make several different versions depending on the options.  I have installed several aftermarket cruise controls on different types of vehicles in the past, and they all worked quite well.  I was looking for the easiest way this time.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||06-13-2001||11:43 PM||||This isn't rocket science but it's not a beginer project either... hook this up wrong and the result could be fatal.<P>The cruise harness is Not installed unless the car came with the option. There is a connector near the ECM for the harness to drop into. This is the only item common to non cruise cars.<P>That means you have to recreate the entire cruise harness. This sounds simple but it's only posible if you have ALLdata or maybe the Helms service book for 87/88. The cruise wiring layout is not available anyplace else except maybe a dealer.<P>You also have to cut connectors from junk cars because they are not available anywhere else. I don't think even the dealers can get them without a major pain... <P>The servo has to be recovered from an FWD DIS motor car. These are the only ones that have the right cable on them so that you can connect them to the top section of the throttle pulley next to the TBI. You have to alter the attachement point on the throttle cable to install the servo cable. Presently that location is a blank. you will also have to fabricate a bracket for the servo.<P>||||reg||1
